	(footprint "PCBedu1:EDU1_DUT_Socket_PGA64_PCB3006-1"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "6dc5d642-f182-41dd-bc1e-86f779462469")
		(at 150 77)
		(descr "64-position female header socket footprint for Proto Advantage PCB3006-1 TQFP-64 adapter carrier board (0.1in / 2.54mm pitch). Pin numbers match EDU1 chip pinout (Chip_pins.xlsx / EDU1_Rebuilt.kicad_sym). Left/bottom/right edges (pins 1-48) confirmed against the PCB3006-1 Pin Out 2 of 4 diagram. Top edge (pins 49-64) corrected: the two staggered rows are offset by one half-pitch (1.27mm), not column-aligned -- pin 64 sits alone at the left end, pin 49 alone at the right end, and 63/62, 61/60, 59/58, 57/56, 55/54, 53/52, 51/50 each share a column in between, per close visual inspection of the datasheet. Each row still holds a uniform 2.54mm pitch internally. Corner-to-corner spacing between the four side groups is a clean design clearance choice, NOT a measurement off the adapter -- verify against the physical board before fabrication.")
